NASty on Debian Trixie (armhf / QNAP TS-228)
============================================

This packaging replaces the upstream NixOS appliance model with Debian
packages and apt-based upgrades.

Architecture
------------
Primary target: armhf (ARMv7 / Realtek RTD1195 on QNAP TS-228).
Packages are Architecture: any / all and can also be built for amd64.

Root filesystem
---------------
Root must be btrfs. On first configure, the `nasty` package runs
`snapper -c root create-config /` when / is btrfs.

Updates
-------
WebUI Update → apt-get upgrade (via nasty-engine).
apt hooks in /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/80nasty-snapper create snapper
pre/post snapshots around dpkg operations.
Generations in the WebUI list snapper snapshots; Switch runs
`snapper rollback <n>` (reboot required).

Build
-----
  apt-get install build-essential debhelper cargo rustc nodejs npm \
    libssl-dev pkg-config clang
  # For TS-228 cross builds from amd64:
  #   dpkg --add-architecture armhf
  #   apt-get install crossbuild-essential-armhf
  #   rustup target add armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf
  dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Install into an existing Trixie rootfs
--------------------------------------
  apt-get install ./nasty-engine_*.deb ./nasty-webui_*.deb ./nasty_*.deb
  systemctl enable --now nasty-metrics nasty-engine
  # Point Caddy at debian/Caddyfile.nasty or merge into /etc/caddy/Caddyfile

Next ports
----------
  * Replace remaining bcachefs storage paths with btrfs (in progress)
  * SMB uses ksmbd (`ksmbd.service`); AD / Time Machine removed
  * WS-Discovery via `wsdd2` (full unit override binds to ksmbd, not Samba smbd)
  * FTP / SFTP / S3 file serving via `rclone serve` (enable under Sharing)
